# Woodpecker campaign working files.
#
# Each of these is created by one step and consumed by a later step of the SAME
# workflow. While they were neither tracked nor ignored, the evidence guard in
# the later step saw them as a dirty tree and refused -- a workflow failing on
# files it had just created itself, reported as though the checkout were dirty.
# The receipts are per-run CI outputs, and the two fixture inputs are built
# from unifi-emu at a pinned commit for a scratch image, so none of them
# belong in the tree.
build/**/*-ci.json
/m3-candidate/
/.woodpecker/fixtures/catalog-acceptance/unifi-emu
/.woodpecker/fixtures/catalog-acceptance/devices.fleet.json
/upgrade-plan-runner
/catalog-controller-differential
/catalog-dependency-publishability
/catalog-unit-differential
/schema-parity

# Executables left at the repository root by `go build ./cmd/<name>`.
#
# Without an -o, go build writes the binary into the working directory named
# after the command's directory. Run from the root -- which is where every
# other go command here is run -- that leaves a multi-megabyte executable
# beside the source, untracked and easy to sweep into a `git add`. One such
# commit added five of them, 19 MB, and they reached a shared branch.
#
# THE FIRST ATTEMPT AT THIS RULE SAT DEAD IN THIS FILE FOR ITS ENTIRE LIFE:
# a missing newline joined it to the line above, so
# `/.woodpecker/fixtures/catalog-acceptance/devices.fleet.json/upgrade-plan-runner`
# was one path matching nothing rather than two matching something. It was split
# and restored in 9c654f56, and /upgrade-plan-runner above is that repair; it
# appears again below because this list is the complete set of cmd/ names and a
# partial one would read as an omission. Nothing noticed for the whole of its
# life, which is why the list below is bound to cmd/ by
# check_stray_binaries_test.go rather than trusted.
/action-gen
/catalog-admission
/catalog-evidence
/catalog-hardware-disposition
/catalog-management-contract
/catalog-migration-recovery
/catalog-migration-verify
/catalog-parity
/catalog-pragmatic-evidence
/catalog-release-ready
/export-gate
/go-unifi-pin
/go-unifi-proxy
/list-policy-scaffold
/list-resource-gen
/m3-dns-qualification
/nested-custom-type-strip
/nested-type-dedup
/policy-scaffold
/provider-spec-compiler
/receipt-gate
/schema-baseline
/schema-behaviour
/sdk-bootstrap
/tree-state
/upgrade-plan-runner
/workspace-provenance
